# One person authors this repository. Every identity the tooling has ever
# committed under is mapped here onto the account's canonical noreply form, so
# `git log`, `git shortlog`, `git blame` and GitHub's contributor list show a
# single author.
#
# This file rewrites nothing. It changes how history is *displayed*, not what is
# stored, so it costs no force-push and invalidates no open branch. Fixing the
# stored author field requires rewriting commits, which is tracked separately.
#
# Rule for tooling in this repo: do NOT pass -c user.name / user.email, do NOT
# set GIT_AUTHOR_NAME / GIT_COMMITTER_NAME, and do NOT add Co-Authored-By
# trailers. The repository's configured identity is the only author there is.

# The two legitimate spellings of the account, and the noreply form both map to.
refusedguy <40535288+refusedguy@users.noreply.github.com>
refusedguy <40535288+refusedguy@users.noreply.github.com> <refusedguy@gmail.com>

